      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;My presentation focuses on Rails Admin, the project which I have developed under the auspices of the Ruby Summer of Code initiative. My involvement in the Ruby Summer of Code project departed from the goal I have shared with both my coworkers and my mentor - that of further increasing the ease and speed of Ruby web application development.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;RailsAdmin was conceived to be built with focus on code readability and extensibility, with the idea that it may one day work with any Rack-based application. RailsAdmin is currently available for use although its 1.0 version has yet to be released - something which is expected to happen by the end of December 2010. The code is available on github for use together with a README and some screenshots which can be consulted here: http://github.com/sferik/rails_admin/&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;RailsAdmin is a Rails engine that provides an easy-to-use interface for managing your data.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
